Q1. You are building a food delivery application. At which stage would you
    prefer using a compiler over an interpreter, and why? Explain based on
    execution speed, error detection and deployment.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ANSWER:

For a food delivery application, I would prefer a COMPILER at the
Production/Deployment stage.

REASON:

1. EXECUTION SPEED:
   -> A compiler translates the entire source code into machine code BEFORE
      execution. So the app runs much faster at runtime.
   -> An interpreter translates line-by-line during execution, making it slower.
   -> In a food delivery app, speed is critical (order placement, real-time
      tracking, payment), so compiled code performs better.

2. ERROR DETECTION:
   -> A compiler detects ALL syntax and type errors BEFORE running the program.
   -> This means the entire codebase is validated at once during compilation.
   -> For a food delivery app, catching errors before deployment prevents
      app crashes for customers during order processing.

3. DEPLOYMENT:
   -> Compiled code produces an executable (.exe / .apk / binary) that can
      be deployed directly without needing the source code on the machine.
   -> This is more secure and efficient for production deployment.
   -> Interpreted code requires the interpreter to be installed on every
      machine, which is not ideal for app distribution.

CONCLUSION:
  -> Use Interpreter during Development (quick testing, line-by-line debugging).
  -> Use Compiler during Production/Deployment (speed, security, efficiency).

  +--------------------+---------------------+----------------------+
  | Feature            | Compiler            | Interpreter          |
  +--------------------+---------------------+----------------------+
  | Translation        | Whole program once  | Line by line         |
  | Speed              | Faster at runtime   | Slower               |
  | Error Detection    | Before execution    | During execution     |
  | Deployment         | Standalone binary   | Needs interpreter    |
  | Best For           | Production apps     | Development/testing  |
  +--------------------+---------------------+----------------------+


