B3. Functions & Pointers - Swap Two Numbers
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ANSWER:

#include <stdio.h>

// Function to swap using pointers (pass-by-reference)
void swapNumbers(int *a, int *b) {
    int temp = *a;
    *a = *b;
    *b = temp;
}

int main() {
    int num1, num2;

    printf("========================================\n");
    printf("         NUMBER SWAP PROGRAM            \n");
    printf("========================================\n");

    printf("Enter first number  : ");
    scanf("%d", &num1);
    printf("Enter second number : ");
    scanf("%d", &num2);

    printf("\nBefore Swap: num1 = %d, num2 = %d\n", num1, num2);

    // Call swap function with addresses (pointers)
    swapNumbers(&num1, &num2);

    printf("After Swap : num1 = %d, num2 = %d\n", num1, num2);
    printf("========================================\n");

    return 0;
}

/*
EXPLANATION -- Why Pass-by-Reference (Pointers) is Necessary:

  In C, function arguments are passed BY VALUE by default.
  This means a COPY of the variable is sent to the function.
  Changes made inside the function do NOT affect the original variables.

  WRONG approach (pass-by-value):
  void swapWrong(int a, int b) {
      int temp = a;
      a = b;
      b = temp;
      // Only swaps local copies! Original num1, num2 unchanged.
  }

  CORRECT approach (pass-by-reference using pointers):
  void swapNumbers(int *a, int *b) {
      int temp = *a;   // dereference pointer to get actual value
      *a = *b;         // change value at memory address of num1
      *b = temp;       // change value at memory address of num2
  }

  -> When we pass &num1 and &num2, we pass the MEMORY ADDRESSES.
  -> Inside the function, *a and *b directly modify the original variables.
  -> So the swap is reflected in main() after the function call.

  MEMORY DIAGRAM:
    num1 at address 1000 --> value: 10
    num2 at address 2000 --> value: 20
    After swap: address 1000 --> 20, address 2000 --> 10
*/

/*
SAMPLE OUTPUT:
  Enter first number  : 10
  Enter second number : 20
  Before Swap: num1 = 10, num2 = 20
  After Swap : num1 = 20, num2 = 10
*/


